    "result_text": "Done. The full build is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`, `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0`), including the new `coreIdempotentRepeat` acceptance test and app startup wiring validation.\n\n## What I implemented\n\n`POST /api/owners` now honours the optional `Idempotency-Key` header: a repeat create with an already-seen key returns the originally created owner with **200** instead of creating a duplicate (which would otherwise 409).\n\nFollowing the project's OfficeFloor function-injection idiom, I added a new entry step and a replay branch to `src/main/resources/officefloor/rest/api/owners.POST.yml`:\n\n- **`checkIdempotency`** (new first step) reads the header and branches via two `@Flow` outputs \u2014 `replay` when the key was already used, `proceed` otherwise. Using two flows with no `next:` (always calling exactly one) makes the either/or branch unambiguous.\n- **`loadStored` \u2192 `respondReplay`** reuses the existing `RespondWithOwner` (200) under `readonly-transaction`, mirroring the `GET /owners/{id}` shape.\n- **`recordIdempotency`** (inserted after `audit`, before the 201 responder) remembers `key \u2192 owner id` once the owner is saved.\n\nNew classes under `rest/function/owner/`:\n- `IdempotencyStore` \u2014 `@Component` singleton mapping key \u2192 owner id (`putIfAbsent`, first-writer-wins).\n- `CheckIdempotencyKey` \u2014 reads `@HttpHeaderParameter(\"Idempotency-Key\")` (injects `null` when absent \u2014 verified via `HttpArgumentManagedObjectSource`, whose value field defaults to `null`), publishes the key, and routes.\n- `IdempotencyKey` \u2014 record holder published as `Out`/read as `@Val` for the recording step.\n- `LoadStoredOwner` \u2014 loads the stored owner by the replayed id.\n- `RecordIdempotencyKey` \u2014 records the mapping (no-op when no key supplied).\n\nKeyless creates (every other endpoint call) are unaffected: `checkIdempotency` simply takes the `proceed` branch into the unchanged validate\u2192\u2026\u2192respond pipeline.",
