    "probe_text": "Here is the complete ordered list of everything applied to `POST /api/owners`, as the code stands. The endpoint (`owners.POST.yml`) wires these steps in sequence; all steps from `validate` onward run inside a single write transaction (`govern: [ transaction ]`), so the whole thing commits once at the end.\n\n## 0. Gate (before any step)\n- **Authorization:** `composition.authorize: hasRole('OWNER_ADMIN')` \u2014 the whole endpoint is rejected (403) for callers without that role.\n\n## 1. `CheckIdempotencyKey`\n- Reads the optional `Idempotency-Key` header and publishes it (as an `IdempotencyKey`, `null` when absent).\n- If the key is present **and** already recorded in `IdempotencyStore`, it **branches to replay**: loads the previously-created owner (`LoadStoredOwner`, read-only txn) and returns it with **200** (`RespondWithOwner`). No new owner is created \u2014 the rest of the pipeline is skipped.\n- Otherwise (new key, or no key) it proceeds to validation.\n\n## 2. `ValidateNewOwner` \u2014 validations, in this internal order\n1. **Address normalization + selection.** If `addressLine1` is non-blank, the structured lines are normalized and the flat `address` is composed from them (`addressLine1` + optional ` ` + `addressLine2`); otherwise the flat `address` is normalized. Normalization = trim, collapse internal whitespace, upper-case, and expand whole-word street abbreviations (`ST\u2192STREET`, `RD\u2192ROAD`, `AVE\u2192AVENUE`). This mutated address is what everything downstream reads.\n2. **Required-field check** (after address normalization): `firstName`, `lastName`, `address`, `city`, `telephone` must be non-blank. Any missing \u2192 **400** (`MissingOwnerFieldsException`, body lists the offending field names).\n3. **Telephone \u2192 E.164 normalization**, written back onto the request. Strips spaces/dashes/brackets; keeps a leading `+`/country code, else assumes `+61` and drops a single leading `0`. Must be 8\u201315 digits, and national length must match the country code (`+61`\u21929, `+1`\u219210). Invalid \u2192 **400** (`InvalidTelephoneException`).\n4. **Email normalization** (optional). Blank/absent \u2192 left unset. Present \u2192 must match the syntactic pattern (\u2192 **400** `InvalidEmailException`), is lower-cased, and its domain must not be on the disposable blocklist `mailinator.com`, `tempmail.com`, `guerrillamail.com` (\u2192 **400** `DisposableEmailDomainException`).\n5. **Postcode validation** (optional). Absent \u2192 accepted. Present \u2192 must be exactly 4 digits and, for a city with a known region, fall in range (NSW 2000\u20132099, VIC 3000\u20133099, QLD 4000\u20134099); unknown-region city accepts any 4-digit code. Malformed/out-of-range \u2192 **400** (`InvalidPostcodeException`).\n6. **Registration-date check** (optional). If supplied and later than the server date (`LocalDate.now()`) \u2192 **400** (`FutureRegistrationDateException`). Back-dating is allowed; absent is allowed.\n\n## 3. `CheckOwnerIdentityUnique` \u2014 duplicate rejection\n- Household identity = SHA-256 over `normalizedLastName|postcode`. If an existing **non-soft-deleted** owner shares this household id \u2192 **409** (`DuplicateOwnerIdentityException`).\n- Bypassed when the request declares `sharesHousehold: true` (allowed through as a legitimate second member).\n\n## 4. `CheckOwnerCityCapacity`\n- Counts existing owners whose city matches case-insensitively. If **\u2265 50** \u2192 **409** (`OwnerCityFullException`).\n\n## 5. `CheckOwnerDailyLimit`\n- Computes the effective registration date (supplied or `now()`), rolls it forward to a business day, and counts owners already stamped with that day. If **\u2265 100** \u2192 **429** (`DailyOwnerLimitException`).\n\n## 6. `BuildOwner` \u2014 side-effect (entity creation)\n- Maps the DTO to an `Owner` and sets `registrationDate` to the effective date **rolled forward to the next business day** (skips weekends and the fixed 2026 public-holiday list).\n\n## 7\u201311. Field-assignment side-effects (all mutate the entity in place, pre-save)\n- **`AssignCustomerCode`:** sets `customerCode = <REGION>-<HASH8>`, region from postcode/city, `HASH8` = first 8 upper-hex of SHA-256 over `normalizedTelephone + lastName`; on collision with an existing code, appends `-<n>` (smallest n \u2265 2).\n- **`AssignMembershipNumber`:** sets `membershipNumber = <customerCode>-M<YY>`, `YY` = last two digits of the fiscal year (starting 1 July) of the adjusted registration date.\n- **`AssignHousehold`:** sets `householdId` (deterministic from last name + postcode).\n- **`AssignNamesakeCount`:** sets `namesakeCount` = count of existing owners sharing first+last name (case-insensitive), excluding the new one.\n- **`AssignPossibleDuplicate`:** sets `possibleDuplicate` / `possibleDuplicateOf`. Flags true (with the lowest matching owner id) when a non-deleted existing owner shares last name + postcode but has a **different** telephone. A declared household member (`sharesHousehold`) is never flagged.\n\n## 12. `SaveOwner` \u2014 side-effect (persistence)\n- `ownerRepository.save(owner)` \u2014 persists the owner and assigns its id.\n\n## 13. `AuditOwnerCreated` \u2014 side-effect (logging)\n- Emits an `AUDIT` logger line: owner id, customerCode, registrationDate, derived membershipLevel, membershipNumber.\n\n## 14. `RecordIdempotencyKey` \u2014 side-effect\n- If a key was supplied, records `key \u2192 owner.id` in `IdempotencyStore` so a later repeat replays this owner. No-op when no key.\n\n## 15. `RespondWithOwnerCreated` \u2014 response\n- Maps to `OwnerDto`, sets `bulkSignupWarning` (true when > 80 owners share the registration day), computes and sets `membershipPoints` and `membershipLevel`, and responds **201 Created** with a `Location: /api/owners/{id}` header.\n\n---\n\n**Escalation mapping** (registered handlers turning the above throws into HTTP statuses): `MissingOwnerFieldsException`, `InvalidTelephoneException`, `InvalidEmailException`, `InvalidPostcodeException`, `FutureRegistrationDateException`, `DisposableEmailDomainException` \u2192 **400**; `DuplicateOwnerIdentityException` \u2192 **409**; `OwnerCityFullException` \u2192 **409**; `DailyOwnerLimitException` \u2192 **429**; plus `DataIntegrityViolationException`, `NotFoundException`, and a catch-all `java.lang.Exception` handler.\n\nOne thing worth flagging: the required-field check in step 2 runs **after** address normalization but the telephone/email/postcode/date validations run after it \u2014 so a blank telephone yields the \"missing fields\" 400, while a malformed one yields the telephone 400."
